course: dictionary
lesson: 12290
title: Convey: messages and carrying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Convey is a word with two meanings. The first is to make an idea, feeling or message known to someone. «Her smile conveyed that she was happy to see us.» Her smile did not say the words, but it showed us she was happy. That is what convey means here.
explain: The second meaning is more formal: to carry or take something from one place to another. «The belt conveys boxes from the factory to the lorry.» The boxes are moved along, so convey means carry here.
explain: When you meet convey, ask: is someone getting a message across, or is something being carried? The words around it show you which meaning fits. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Convey means to make an idea, feeling or message known to someone.
fact: Convey can also mean to carry or take something from one place to another. This meaning is more formal.
fact: Convey is a verb, so it changes: conveys, conveyed, conveying.
fact: Pipes convey water, and blood vessels convey blood, because they carry it along.
fact: A conveyor belt is a moving belt that carries things, such as in a factory or at an airport.
exercise: «Her smile conveyed that she was happy to see us.» What does conveyed mean here? | Carried her smile across the room | Hid her feelings | *Made her happiness known | Was angry at us
exercise: «Blood vessels convey blood around the body.» What does convey mean here? | *Carry from one place to another | Wash something clean | Make a message known | Stop something from moving
exercise: Which phrase means a belt that carries things along? | *Conveyor belt | Message belt | Convey a feeling | Convey a message
test: «The poet uses the grey sky to convey sadness.» What is conveyed to the reader? | Some grey clouds in the sky | *A feeling of sadness | A map of the town | A new poem about the sea
test: «The pipes convey water to every house on the street.» What is the best meaning of convey here? | Freeze hard in the cold | Speak loudly to people | Make a feeling known | *Carry from one place to another
exam: Which sentence uses convey to mean to make a message known? | *The card will convey our thanks to Grandma. | The conveyor belt stopped suddenly. | The pipes convey gas to the kitchen. | The lorry will convey the crates to the port.
